##### Operational Rationale for 3D Medical Scan Profile Auditing

The inclusion of 3D Medical Scan Profiles and Clinical Imaging Files in the preservation hold checklist addresses a specific operational vulnerability: the risk of unverified clinical or psychological misclassifications being entered into administrative or judicial records without proper assessment. Auditors must evaluate FDA compliance, voxel propagation models, and terahertz (t-ray) scanning integrity—recovering frequency data from damaged or decayed records—to ensure that medical imaging and diagnostic profiles are scientifically authentic. This prevents administrative entities from utilizing improper medical labels to bypass due process or justify unauthorized institutional custody.

